  "result": "Namespaces are implemented and all 8 tests pass. Nothing was changed outside `kvstore/store.py`.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **Schema:** the SQLite table now has an `ns` column with a composite `(ns, key)` primary key, so the same key can hold different values per namespace. Data still lives in the single file.\n- **Existing methods:** `set`, `get`, `delete`, and `keys` gained `ns: str = \"default\"` and filter every query by namespace. Upsert conflict handling targets the `(ns, key)` pair.\n- **New methods:** `count(ns)` returns the row count for one namespace. `namespaces()` returns the sorted distinct namespace names that have at least one row, so a namespace disappears once its last key is deleted.\n- **Migration:** on open, if the file has the old single-key `kv` table, its rows are moved into the `default` namespace. This isn't covered by the tests, so I verified it with a hand-built legacy file and confirmed no side files remain after close.\n\n**Verification**\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n8 passed in 0.08s\n```",
